WEBVTT

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:19.910
The advice to take life less seriously, given to one who takes life seriously,
 may, or may not, at times, be necessary, or unnecessary.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.210
<i>The advice to take life less seriously, 
given to one who takes life seriously,</i>

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.550
<i>may, or may not, at times, be 
necessary, or unnecessary.</i>

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.910
<b>Episode 9</b>

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.910
<b>Akutagawa-kun's 
Errands</b>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.930
<b>Dazai-san</b>

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.920
It's D-Dazai-san!

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.950
Hello? It's me.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:38.180
Akutagawa-kun?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.650
Good, I finally got through.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.720
There's something I wanted to ask you to do.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:46.430
For you, Dazai-san,
 I would jump off an airship.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.500
It doesn't sound like a 
joke when you say that.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.840
Could you go shopping for me?

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.950
Don't worry. It's easy to find, even for you.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.600
<i>Dazai-san asked me to do something!</i>

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.270
<i>Dazai-san is counting on me!</i>

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.030
Do you have a notepad handy?

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.090
First...

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:09.590
<b>Notes</b>

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.780
<i>I shall complete this errand!</i>

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.580
<i>Even if it costs me everything I have!</i>

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.620
Hey.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.560
Akutagawa-senpai.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.930
I didn't expect to run into you here.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.080
Higuchi.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.610
What's the note?

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.930
Is that a shopping list?

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:22.850
Why are you doing that, Senpai?

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.470
I'll do it for you.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.970
You can go back.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:26.900
Don't touch it!

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.480
These are my errands!

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.710
R-Right.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:30.950
I'm sorry.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.700
<i>Errands?</i>

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.700
<b>Item 1: Toilet paper</b>

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.210
<b>Toilet 
Paper</b>

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.210
<b>Double</b>

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.210
<b>Single</b>

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.310
<i>Single? Double?</i>

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.380
<i>What is that?</i>

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.200
<i>Are there no triples?</i>

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.710
<b>For bidets</b>

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.330
<i>For bidets?</i>

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.320
<i>Is Dazai-san a bidet man?</i>

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:56.640
<i>I must choose paper fit 
for Dazai-san's buttocks.</i>

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.220
<b>Serious Business</b>

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.720
<b>Two Hours Later</b>

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.710
<i>All right, next.</i>

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.610
Akutagawa.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:06.040
I have no business with you, weretiger.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.290
Begone immediately.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.690
I have business here.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.980
I don't have time to waste on you.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:16.720
Savor your fortune and get out of my sight!

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.030
Fine, fine. I get it.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.330
I get it. Jeez.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:25.240
Yummy
 Milk

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:25.240
<i>Akutagawa completed his 
errands with diligence.</i>

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.590
<i>I must choose the freshest milk.</i>

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>Item 2: Milk</b>

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:33.500
<b>Yokohama Snacks</b>

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.100
<i>That other shop was cheaper.</i>

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.170
<i>I'll go back there.</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.500
<b>Item 3: Snacks</b>

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.800
<i>There's a triple point bonus today.</i>

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.280
<b>Item 4: Drug Store</b>

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.500
<i>I got a membership card</i>

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.370
<i>under Dazai-san's name.</i>

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.240
<b>Don't do this.</b>

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.260
<i>And so...</i>

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.890
<i>He completed all of his errands.</i>

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.280
<i>Hello?</i>

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.980
I-It's me. Akutagawa.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:02:59.940
I've completed everything as instructed.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.430
<i>Thanks, man! You're awesome.</i>

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.270
I only did what was expected.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.900
<i>Lastly, could you give that 
stuff to Atsushi-kun?</i>

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:12.070
<i>They're supplies for the Agency.</i>

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.190
<i>Thanks!</i>

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.770
Today's a disaster.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.080
Damn it... It's all Akutagawa's fault.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.090
Why do I have to deal with this?

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:27.100
There you are!

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:27.920
Akutagawa!

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.540
Wh-What the...?

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.290
What's up with all that stuff?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.180
Weretiger...

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.880
I was looking for you!

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.770
Why did you wander off?!

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.370
I got out of your sight, like you wanted.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.950
<b>Wan!</b>

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.950
<b>Shorts</b>

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:53.290
I like curry udon, but it's 
my white shirt's mortal enemy.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.720
I hear you're in a predicament, Atsushi-kun.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.210
I'll take care of the curry udon!

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.870
Hey there! I'm Dazai Osamu!

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.490
Oh, you're right.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.520
You're wearing a curry udon-colored coat.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.210
So, may I have this bowl of curry udon?

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.160
Sure.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.890
You're hungry, huh?

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.620
Thank you!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.940
Wait, please, Dazai-san!

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.980
Please don't consume any curry 
udon that the weretiger prepares!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.650
I shall have it all, for your sake!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.660
Your clothes would be in danger, too!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:27.080
How'd you even get up to the window?

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.030
Do you have any idea what floor this is?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.730
Yum.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.070
Dazai-san!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.750
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.750
<b>The Mafia Member
 Who Doesn't Kill</b>

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.510
They say fools and smoke share 
an affinity for high places.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.870
Hey! I heard that, Akutagawa!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.660
He's getting a balloon.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.640
They gave me one at the market, 
but I let it get away.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.530
Here you go.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.820
I got it back.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.400
See? An adorable tiger balloon.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.900
<b>Urgh</b>

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.180
Rashoumon!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.690
Dude!

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.270
Dude!

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.780
It ticked me off.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.120
What are you, a short-tempered young'un?!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.160
Aren't you?

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.530
Damn it.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.300
You'd better be keeping 
your promise not to kill.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.580
If you break it, I'm never 
going to challenge you.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.080
That one doesn't count.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.850
<i>Damn that Akutagawa...</i>

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:30.790
<i>The balloon...</i>

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.360
<i>My tiger!</i>

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.430
<i>I mean...</i>

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.940
<i>What's he looking at?</i>

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.310
Be careful.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.300
<i>He's so kind!</i>

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.440
<i>No, that must have been a whim.</i>

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.450
A procession of ants.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.950
This won't end well.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.840
<i>He's redirecting the 
procession with sugar!</i>

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.460
<i>No, this must be a trap to lure 
the ants into the ways of evil.</i>

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:13.020
Sow plant seeds, water them, and raise them.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.150
This ought to help the 
insects in the future.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.980
<i>Something's not right.</i>

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:21.490
<i>He must be plotting to capture insects.</i>

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.980
<b>Suuuuck</b>

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.980
A mosquito on my hand!

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:28.030
Very well.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:29.320
Feed.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.730
<i>Akutagawa looks like he's 
just given up on everything.</i>

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.850
<i>Come on, Akutagawa,</i>

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.980
<i>When they say, "wouldn't even kill an insect," 
it's just a figure of speech.</i>

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:43.000
<b>Beware 
of Stalkers</b>

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.740
Though, I guess it's all good if he's 
going to be kind to insects ,<i>as well</i>.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.040
Hey!

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:51.860
You're doing pretty well.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.360
I bought some pork buns.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:07:00.350
<b>Kishiken</b>

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.130
Here.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.460
Have them.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.670
I've kinda been doubting you.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:06:58.540
I'm, uh...

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.360
Sorry.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.600
<b>Irk</b>

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:02.670
Rashoumon!

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.130
Pig!

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.890
What's wrong with you?!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.440
<b>My ability acted 
up on its own</b>

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.530
I still can't trust you!

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.200
You aren't getting any of this.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.620
<b>Episode 11</b>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.620
<b>Forming a Duo 
With <i>Him</i></b>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.620
<b>The Serious
 Part</b>

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.640
<i>Dazai-san...</i>

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.550
<i>is laying on the ground!</i>

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.060
I want to become a marshmallow.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.200
Dazai-san!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.290
Preferably a s'more.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.800
<i>A marshmallow?!</i>

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.020
<i>What metaphor is this?</i>

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.650
<i>Am I not capable of making even the 
slightest sense of his thought process?</i>

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.570
Oh, it's you.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.170
I'm trying to accomplish my dream right now.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.110
Your dream?

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.280
A man of my fortitude eventually 
longs to become a marshmallow.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.500
<i>I see.</i>

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.290
See?

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.250
Aren't I starting to look 
like a marshmallow?

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.010
See? Squeeeze.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.510
Squeeeze.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.790
I see it!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.280
Yay!

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.380
You can become anything if you try!

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.610
What? No way!

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:11.940
Akutagawa, you dummy!

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.400
Humans don't turn into marshmallows!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.850
That exchange made it clear...

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.270
that Atsushi-kun is far superior to you.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.390
How was that exchange inferior 
to one with the weretiger?!

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.660
You don't know how to take jabs!

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.650
Jabs?

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.950
It's a terrifying skill, granting 
one the ability to control the room

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:34.150
in response to astute 
situational decision-making.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.150
And that's why I've brought 
Atsushi-kun here.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:38.520
Akutagawa!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:42.090
I came here because I was 
promised a sweet snack.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.390
Oh, I was talking about me.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.410
Hurk.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.100
<i>Wretched tiger rug, 
unceasingly rude to Dazai-san...</i>

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.800
<i>I ought to dice him up now!</i>

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.440
Hey! What was that for?!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.290
You grazed me!

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.330
I'm practicing taking jabs.

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.170
That was more of a lethal stab than a jab!

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:04.880
Akutagawa-kun is practicing 
taking jabs right now.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.160
You're messing with him again, aren't you?

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.760
You're going to get in trouble 
for wasting time again.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.080
I'm not wasting time.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.370
I'm dashing toward my goal.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:15.690
Rashoumon!

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:17.290
Stop it! Jeez!

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:18.600
Use your words!

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.400
Coward.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.590
I will not kill!

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.840
You're set on doing everything <i>but</i> killing.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:27.230
When you take a jab,

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.090
you're supposed to slap someone 
with your hand, and say, "Bruh!"

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.860
I'm going to try becoming a 
toasted steam bun this time.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:34.850
Like the Gunma specialty.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:37.450
I'm getting toasty. Turn me over.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:38.210
Yes, sir.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.410
That's it.

00:09:39.410 --> 00:09:41.390
Make sure you cook evenly.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.720
Don't forget the miso sauce.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.010
Bruh!

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.010
That's it!

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.200
I knew it!

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.470
Akutagawa-kun, the natural airhead,

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.950
and straight-man Atsushi-kun, 
with the supreme jabs!

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:56.230
The two of you will win a 
comedy contest together!

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:57.600
Hey, everyone!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.310
I've been hooked on cooking lately.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:02.830
I'm thinking of making you something, too.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.870
Is there anything you want?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.750
I have nothing to say to you.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.920
We have to talk, or we 
wouldn't be doing comedy!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.460
C'mon, gimme a break!

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.950
Here's your break!

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:37.950
Ouch!

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:43.330
In fact, I made those two who they are now.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:43.950
I see...

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.370
Bruh!
